# do not delete me
#
# Git tracks files, not directories, so this directory would vanish from
# the next clone without a file in it. This is that file. It ignores
# nothing on purpose — see `keepMarker` in schemas/cat-harness.ts.
#
# session-marks/
# Whether anybody has LOOKED at the session listing — one file,
# `session-listing.json`, carrying when it was read, by which session, how
# many rows it carried and how many findings that run produced. Bean `rq8s`,
# the owner's ruling 2026-09-23. `check:session-staleness` cannot fetch its
# own input: probed from inside a session container,
# `api.anthropic.com/v1/sessions` is 401 and `claude.ai/api/code/sessions`
# is 403, so `list_sessions` is an MCP tool an AGENT holds and the
# session-start sweep asks for the listing by name. That is a rule in prose,
# and a session that skips it left NO TRACE — the next sweep could not tell
# a skip from a clean run, which is `1xhc`'s "a gate that does not fire is
# indistinguishable from one that passed" committed inside the fix for it.
# This is the trace, so the sweep says never-checked, stale or fresh rather
# than saying nothing three ways. A SIBLING of `issue-marks` rather than
# part of it: that graph holds marks about ISSUES, and widening it would
# rename a declared graph every consumer resolves against. Separate from the
# `session-state` kind too, which is a session's OWN context (its actor, its
# open instances, what it waits on) and has no directory yet by design —
# this is repository-wide and says nothing about any session's position. THE
# FINDING COUNT IS A SNAPSHOT: `rq8s` asserted a live-system reading as fact
# and it was false four hours later, so a consumer rendering the number as a
# current total has reproduced the defect. `state`, and SCOPE IS
# `repository` for the reason `issue-marks` and `interaction` state: without
# it the path resolves against the INSTANCE, and `harness:dirs` then creates
# an empty instance-level directory to satisfy the declaration —
# declared-but-absent turned into declared-and-empty, the `dh4f` false pass
# wearing a tidier face.
